a maximum. A feasible positive triple exists (as exhibited below), so the maximum is positive and occurs in the interior. Lagrange multipliers give\n\\[\nyz=\\lambda+\\mu(y+z),\\quad\nxz=\\lambda+\\mu(x+z),\\quad\nxy=\\lambda+\\mu(x+y).\n\\]\nSubtracting yields\n\\[\n(y-x)(z-\\mu)=(z-y)(x-\\mu)=(x-z)(y-\\mu)=0.\n\\]\nIf all three variables were distinct, these equations would force \\(x=y=z=\\mu\\), a contradiction. Hence two variables are equal.\n\nSet \\(x=y=a\\), \\(z=b\\). Then\n\\[\n2a+b=9,\\qquad a^2+2ab=14,\n\\]\nso\n\\[\n3a^2-18a+14=0.\n\\]\nThe only solution with \\(a,b>0\\) is\n\\[\na=3-\\frac{\\sqrt{39}}3,\\qquad\nb=3+\\frac{2\\sqrt{39}}3.\n\\]\n(The other root gives \\(b<0\\).) Consequently this triple maximizes the product and minimizes the expression. Its value is\n\\[\na+2\\frac{a^2+b^2}{a+b}\n=15+\\frac{\\sqrt{39}}3-\\frac{4+12\\sqrt{39}}{18+\\sqrt{39}}\n=\\frac{1557-39\\sqrt{39}}{95}.\n\\]\n\nFinal answer: \\(\\displaystyle \\boxed{\\frac{1557-39\\sqrt{39}}{95}}\\)."}],"phase":"final_answer","role":"assistant"}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"presence_penalty":0,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":"24h","reasoning":{"context":"all_turns","effort":"medium","mode":"standard","summary":null},"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"default","store":false,"temperature":1,"text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"medium"},"tool_choice":"auto","tool_usage":{"image_gen":{"input_tokens":0,"input_tokens_details":{"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":0},"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":{"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":0},"total_tokens":0},"web_search":{"num_requests":0}},"tools":[],"top_logprobs":0,"top_p":0.98,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":176,"input_tokens_details":{"cache_write_tokens":0,"cached_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1526,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1034},"total_tokens":1702},"user":null,"metadata":{}}
